{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_663veegfouwmgmc6amjazcvxdcy6heesfgyyiueeqlgfpy6fwwia","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both debug and release builds compile cleanly. The translation:\n\n**Implementation summary:**\n\n1. **`compute_indexes`** (helper): Mirrors the C function's logic. For MOTOROLA (big-endian), it walks down `len-1` bits from `startbit`, jumping `+15` whenever it crosses a byte boundary at bit 0. For INTEL (little-endian), it computes `msb = startbit + len - 1`.\n\n2. **`frame_to_local`** (helper): Builds an 8-byte little-endian buffer. For MOTOROLA, frame bytes are read in reverse order (lsb→msb byte indexes count down). For INTEL, they're copied in forward order. Then converted via `u64::from_le_bytes`.\n\n3. **`low_mask`** (helper): Computes `(1 << len) - 1` safely, returning `u64::MAX` when `len == 64` to avoid undefined-behavior shift.\n\n4. **`extract`**: Shifts right by `offset_lsb`, masks to `len` bits, and applies sign extension when `signedness == SIGNED` and the top bit of the field is set.\n\n5. **`insert`**: Reads the original chunk, clears the target bits with `erase_mask`, ORs in the new value, then writes the resulting bytes back to the frame using `to_le_bytes` (reversed order for MOTOROLA).\n\n6. **`encode_*` / `decode_*`**: Apply the `(value - offset) / factor` and `(value * factor) + offset` transforms exactly as in C, preserving the same intermediate i64/u64 casts that affect rounding/wrap-around behavior.\n\nNo `unsafe`, no FFI, no remaining `unimplemented!()` placeholders."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":234,"cache_read_input_tokens":47338,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":234,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8f484d63-432e-42c6-9e3f-fdb7436d857e","